    "description": "In this video, Chef John shows you how to make coffee granita, a refreshing frozen Italian treat. If you have freshly brewed coffee and white sugar, you can make this recipe. After stirring until the sugar is completely dissolved, transfer the coffee to a baking dish and let it sit in the freezer for over an hour. Once the dish is partially frozen, break up the frozen pieces and repeat this process in the freezer every 30 minutes until it has the proper crystalized texture. Whether you have it in the morning for breakfast or on a hot summer’s day, this decadent dessert is sweet and smooth!",
